  "sections": [
    {
      "block_id": "h1-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Product Surface: Rig MVP for VSCodium",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This document defines the user experience and visual components of the Rig Relay extension.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Primary Surfaces",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "A. The \"Mission Control\" Sidebar (Webview View)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "*   **Chat Interface**: Minimalist prompt input and response stream. *   **Turn Status**: Visual indicator of the current agent turn (Thinking, Running Tool, Waiting for Approval). *   **Context Indicator**: Compact list of files currently being used as context (with \"remove\" buttons).",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "B. The \"Evidence Rail\" (Tree View)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "*   List of recent sessions and their associated receipts. *   Clicking a receipt opens a custom \"Receipt Viewer\" (read-only document) showing the rationale and verifiable evidence.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "C. The \"Governance Bar\" (Status Bar)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "*   Current Rig status (Ready, Active, Blocked). *   Workspace lane indicator (e.g., \"Lane: main\" or \"Lane: rig-patch-001\").",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "D. The \"Patch Review\" Surface (Native Diff View)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "*   When an agent proposes a change, Rig triggers a native VSCodium Diff view. *   Floating \"Approve\" / \"Reject\" buttons inside the diff surface or as a notification toast.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Competitive Positioning",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-13",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Feature",
        "Like Antigravity / Cursor",
        "Unlike Antigravity (The Rig Wedge)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "**Inline Edit**",
          "Yes, via diff view.",
          "Always governed; requires approval by default."
        ],
        [
          "**Context**",
          "Yes, auto-detects files.",
          "Verifiable: Every byte of context is recorded in a receipt."
        ],
        [
          "**Tools**",
          "Yes, runs bash/ls.",
          "Deterministic: Tools are hardened and permissioned."
        ],
        [
          "**Workspace**",
          "Yes, uses project root.",
          "Lane-based: Heavy use of worktrees to isolate agent noise."
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-14",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Minimum Visibility Rules",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "*   **Default Visible**: Mission Control Sidebar, Governance Bar. *   **Hidden behind commands**: Full Receipt Browser, Debug logs, Configuration. *   **Do Not Build Yet**: AI-driven file tree manipulation, generic multi-agent chat, auto-commit.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Design Aesthetics",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "*   **Phosphor Monochrome**: Use the green-phosphor palette for the Webview components to maintain the Rig brand identity. *   **Bauhaus Functional**: Avoid \"glass\" or \"glow\" effects in the editor; stick to sharp, functional, high-contrast layouts that match VSCodium's native feel.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    }
  ],
